      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I recently saw this happen on a very fast time scale (minutes) on a newer world using persistence and in this case, it was caused by log entries for an exception being logged every frame. This could happen in any kind of world new or old with or without persistence if there is anything (ANYTHING) which creates a log entry every frame, and for worlds which haven't been updated in a while, if there is some sort of client change which could cause a previously quiet error to now cause a log entry to be made every frame, there you go. This may or may not be the exact cause of this specific issue, but it is one of possibly many ways for a similar issue to happen.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
